---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import coverage from '../../reports/coverage.json';
import {href,database} from '../lib/data';
---
<Layout title="Sources, coverage & privacy"><div class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">REFERENCE STANDARDS</p><h1>Sources, coverage & privacy</h1><p>This wiki separates extracted facts, developer descriptions and guide recommendations. It has no account service or game-save integration.</p></div><article class="prose"><h2>What this snapshot covers</h2><p>The approved local catalog is generated from game {database.gameVersion}. It documents {coverage.entries.toLocaleString()} records. Counts include card tiers and combat reference templates, so they are not counts of distinct recruitable families.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Documented</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(coverage.categories).map(([category,count])=><tr><td><a href={href(`${category}/`)}>{category}</a></td><td>{count}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><h2>How to read the evidence</h2><p>Card statistics, pack membership, costs and ability text are extracted from source modules. Card descriptions are the developer’s text. Combat formulas are verified against the shared engine. Guide recommendations reason from those rules and are not presented as tested optimal builds.</p><p>Every entity lists its source modules. The maintenance pipeline generates a proposed snapshot and change report. Approved hashes prevent an unreviewed extraction or asset change from entering a build.</p><h2>Spoiler controls</h2><p>Story titles, overviews, boss identities and hidden rewards have click-to-reveal controls. Search and galleries hide spoiler records by default. Protected entity pages use generic metadata and request no indexing. Revealing spoilers in one tool does not reveal them across every page.</p><h2>Known limits and investigations</h2><ul>{coverage.investigations.map(i=><li>{i}</li>)}</ul><p>{coverage.missingArt.length} templates have no resolved official foreground. Their pages state this and use an available faction background. Enemy values are templates before encounter scaling. Boss and guest templates are not automatically recruitable.</p><h2>Your data stays on this device</h2><p>Collection, achievement, journey and team-planning state uses this browser’s local storage. There is no login, payment API or backend in the wiki. Page views are counted anonymously with GoatCounter, which sets no cookies and stores no personal data; the visitor total in the footer comes from it. The checklist export lets you keep a copy. Clearing browser storage removes local state.</p><p>The wiki links to Steam; opening that link visits Steam under its own policies. The wiki does not process purchases or connect to game servers.</p><h2>Updates and corrections</h2><p>Manually authored guides live separately from generated data. New or changed game content requires a fresh audit, candidate review, production build and link checks before approved deployment. Unreleased DLC never becomes public merely because files exist in the source tree.</p></article></Layout>
